Secondly, [ " Shifts And CTRL Notes " ]
1. Shifts
when you try to learn to play a song which you see the caps notes
they are the most annoying things and the most important things about the sheets
When you see a chord like this : [WOru]
so, the chords you see have caplocks, wihich is really annoying. Here's how to press it:
- You Can Press The [WO] first and press [ru] so it's gonna be very easy for you
- Disadvantage things : It won't make the pieces sound 100% perfection, it only helps you to press it properly
- you can do it backwards ( not really recommended )

Examples : [$Qpsg] → [$Q] [psg]
           [4qOSH] → [OSH] [4q]
2. CTRL notes
Next is CTRL notes, which is really important to a song
So, when you see the notes that contains this :_', it means you're seeing the ctrl notes
Then how to do it ?
when you see a chord like this : [:9'4psg]
- Press CTRL 9 first and press [4psg]
- If You're in Piano Haven game, you can easily make it 100% perfection by pressting F1 key To F8 Key which is very useful 
- Not recommended if you're trying to press it backwards

Examples : [:e'6psfj] → CTRL e [6psfj]
           [:q'5oafh] → CTRL q [5oafh]
